  "question": {
    "text": "If a tangent to the ellipse <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;meets the tangents at the extremities of its major axis at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;then the circle with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> as diameter passes through the point."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"assets\\st0062_0be67cad1256.png\" style=\"width: 452px; height: 254px;\" /></p><p>We have,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Equation of tangent is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>cot</mi><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Equation of required circle will be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cot</mi><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>tan</mi><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>cot</mi><mfrac><mi>&#952;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> satisfies the above equation.</p>"
  }
}